        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T17:23:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "/** Bluetooth Device Type */\ntypedef enum {\n  BT_DEVICE_DEVTYPE_BREDR \u003d 0x1,\n  BT_DEVICE_DEVTYPE_BLE,\n  BT_DEVICE_DEVTYPE_DUAL\n} bt_device_type_t;\n\nI see a place where sizeof(bt_device_type_t) is used.  It looks like the size of this enum is ambiguous.  I think we should make the size the same everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "58df8c6d_c099563f",
      "revId": "2109b3ffecb17a287e8315fa0d2ede81020a3445",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53bfc38b_2e5a7b2d",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_storage.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 316,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T17:58:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems like the spec of c++ doesn\u0027t guarantee the size of enum. It only says \"at least as big as an int\". \n\nHow about we always use 1 byte, then cast the data back at the caller level?",
      "parentUuid": "338ab5b7_f7ec084b",
      "revId": "2109b3ffecb17a287e8315fa0d2ede81020a3445",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b446f80_52c91439",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_storage.cc",
